<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Wafid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1008">1008</a>–<a href="/years/1074">1074</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Wafid (1008–1074) was an Andalusi physician, pharmacologist and agronomist at the court of al-Mamun of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a>. He wrote a treatise on simple drugs, later translated into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, and a work on agriculture. He laid out the royal garden of Toledo, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">Huerta</a> del Rey, one of the earliest botanical gardens in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-wafid.jpg" alt="Ibn Wafid" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gotha,_Ms._oriental_A_72_fol.11v-12r_Ibn_W%C4%81fid_Kit%C4%81b_al-Adwiya_al-Mufrada_excerpt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
